{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1349346-movement-um-how","id":1349346,"title":"Movement. Um... how?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-18T08:55:53-08:00","id":1349346,"title":"Movement. Um... how?","content":"I just ran my first Exalted 3e game. It generally went very well... but combat movement was something of a sticking point. I thought I understood Range Bands as roughly analogous to Zones in Fate-- dividing the battlefield into abstract areas within which exact positioning was unimportant. The once/round reflexive movement action made sense; Disengage made sense; weapon ranges made sense... but Rush kind of didn't. And what's more, I didn't see any way for characters to move multiple range bands in a direction that <i>wasn't </i>towards an enemy. At one point a character wanted to run from the siege weapons they'd set up on the hill outside of town (one range band/zone), through the town square (another range band/zone), and get inside the inn (a third range band/zone). I allowed it at the cost of their combat action for the turn, but... was that right? Was that supposed to be impossible? How d<i>o </i><i>you </i>keep track of this stuff when there are lots of characters on the battlefield?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T09:11:45-08:00","id":1349351,"title":"","content":"Would that be a Dex+Atheltics roll, difficulty how difficult the journey was (enemies, rough terrain, obstructions, with a bonus for charms or a relevant mount) and how possible it was to get there in the space of pne rpund by sprinting without taking other actions? Opposed rolls if someone was chasing them / trying to get close enough to get into combat range. <br /> <br /> Combat movement rolls represent opponents dodging and weaving around one another. If there is nobody actively engaged with the player, surely those actions aren't necessary?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8877-mrfamiliar","name":"MrFamiliar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T09:36:09-08:00","id":1349354,"title":"","content":"Okay, so, Exalted movement is a really complex but ultimately pretty balanced system to movement. Unlike DnD where an archer who\u2019s a bit faster than a melee fighter can pretty well just endlessly kite as long as terrain permits*, exalted movement is designed so that archers who want to keep away always get the chance to do so, and rushing fighters who want to get in close always get a chance to do so as well. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s why you need to aim from medium range, and aim can\u2019t be combined with movement of any kind. It\u2019s also the reason that only with powerful charms can you move multiple range bands in a turn. The basic idea is like this:<br /> <br /> <br /> Disengage is used when you\u2019re in close to get away and still fight. If you disengage successfully you\u2019re rewarded with at least one turn where you get to attack from range. The thing is, if you disengage with somebody and then they use their reflexive move on their turn to follow you, you don\u2019t get that turn, they just close back in. to ensure you get it, if somebody follows you then you get to move back again, fleeing them. <br /> <br /> The rush is the opposite of that. Winning a rush instead ensures that the rusher will get their next turn in close combat, if they want to. It doesn\u2019t move you right away because then somebody fleeing with a disengage might win their disengage and then just get immediately rushed and lose the advantage of their successful disengage. So instead the rush maneuver just makes sure that you\u2019re going to stay at short range no matter what until your next turn, upon which you can move in and close the distance again.<br /> <br /> As soon as you start introducing double moves into the system a lot of it falls apart. <br /> <br /> Also as an aside, range bands are kind of like zones, but it\u2019s worth while to also determine what kind of terrain and stuff separates those zones. For example difficult terrain will take two turns to move through, and it may be possible that neither the area you\u2019re moving to, or from, is difficult terrain, but might be separated by fortifications or climbing a ladder or something.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *which due to DnD dungeon style maps is way less a problem than it sounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T10:38:11-08:00","id":1349364,"title":"","content":"Rush lets you move two range bands (one Reflexively, one as your combat action when the other party moves away). So as long as you're not running toward or away from an opponent, I don't think it's unbalanced to trade a combat action to move another range band.<br /> <br /> I certainly wouldn't let them move THREE range bands. And if you're going towards a fleeing or away from a pursuing opponent then that's clearly unbalanced. But crossing scenery to get stuck in to the action quicker is firmly hand-wavium territory. If you can sprint two range bands towards an archer you can sprint two range bands towards a tavern.<br /> <br /> Keeping track, I've been using a notepad and battlemap (holla at the good people who make Battle Systems Terrain -- that stuff is amazing). Poker chips to track Essence and Willpower, D10s (one on a Carcasson scoreboard and dozens in multicolored popcorn bowls) to track Initiative. There's a lot to keep track of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-18-2019, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T10:47:41-08:00","id":1349365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1349346-movement-um-how?p=1349364#post1349364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rush lets you move two range bands (one Reflexively, one as your combat action). So as long as you're not running toward or away from an opponent, I don't think it's unbalanced to trade a combat action to move another range band.<br /> <br /> I certainly wouldn't let them move THREE range bands. And if you're going towards a fleeing or away from a pursuing opponent then that's clearly unbalanced. But crossing scenery to get stuck in to the action quicker is firmly hand-wavium territory. If you can sprint two range bands towards an archer you can sprint two range bands towards a tavern.<br /> <br /> Keeping track, I've been using a notepad and battlemap (holla at the good people who make Battle Systems Terrain -- that stuff is amazing). Poker chips to track Essence and Willpower, D10s (one on a Carcasson scoreboard and dozens in multicolored popcorn bowls) to track Initiative. There's a lot to keep track of.</div> </div> </div> </div>I might be mistaken but I'm pretty sure Rush doesn't make you move 2 range bands. It makes you move the next time the opponent you rush moves, and that's all. You can use your normal movement action to move a second time though.<br /> <br /> Btw, what happened if you rush someone while you are already engaged to someone else ? Can you ? Must you disengage first ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T10:59:03-08:00","id":1349371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1349346-movement-um-how?p=1349365#post1349365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I might be mistaken but I'm pretty sure Rush doesn't make you move 2 range bands. It makes you move the next time the opponent you rush moves, and that's all. You can use your normal movement action to move a second time though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. Which is moving twice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Btw, what happened if you rush someone while you are already engaged to someone else ? Can you ? Must you disengage first ? </div> </div> </div><s>The devs clarified that you only can't use the Reflexive Move (movement action) when embattled, so I guess Rushing works?</s><br /> <br /> I really don't know about this one. Charms which move you, just move you. No need to Disengage. Rush... I really don't know.<br /> <br /> [Edit]<br /> <br /> Nope, right the first time. Rush away: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1073429#post1073429\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...29#post1073429</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-18-2019, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T10:59:53-08:00","id":1349372,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Rush is only for chasing people who are running away.<br /> It doesn't work for trying to run really fast towards someone standing still. Or towards scenery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T11:12:33-08:00","id":1349382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1349346-movement-um-how?p=1349372#post1349372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Rush is only for chasing people who are running away.<br /> It doesn't work for trying to run really fast towards someone standing still. Or towards scenery.</div> </div> </div> </div>For someone standing still is a balance concern, DrLoveMonkey has already laid that out in full.<br /> <br /> Running really fast towards scenery... so long as you're not trying to cheese the system, this is explicitly a house rule and not RAW, I don't see the issue with double moving. Not canon, absolutely. But it doesn't break anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T12:24:04-08:00","id":1349399,"title":"","content":"Outside of combat that kind of thing should just be a roll or an extended roll, then again outside of combat you often don\u2019t use range bands. Moving twice in a single turn isn\u2019t in and of itself imbalanced. For a lot of cases though it really changes the dynamic. For instance charging a fortification covered with archers SHOULD allow for at least one turn where you\u2019re at short range and they can freely shoot you before you close in. Normally if you\u2019re at medium range they can aim at you, and then the best you can do is close into short where they get to shoot you with their aim bonus, and then you can leap in, but they do get that shot. As long as you\u2019re moving between range bands where ranged/melee fighters don\u2019t really care it should be okay. <br /> <br /> Also there\u2019s one other type of movement that hasn\u2019t been mentioned, and that\u2019s the Withdraw action, which also lets you move twice in a turn in order to escape from combat. Which is an extended roll that costs 10i per round.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T12:40:57-08:00","id":1349411,"title":"","content":"(A common mistake is that rush/disengage/withdraw lets you move twice in a turn. It doesn't. It could let you move twice in a round, but one of those movement actions is outside of your turn. There's no way to use normal movement actions to move two range bands on your turn. Your reflexive movement cannot be combined with another movement unless specifically stated. It's specifically stated in the Rush action because the reflexive movement is necessary to close in on the enemy (you need to move reflexively from medium to short to activate the rush, but you're still at short for the duration of the round---the rush only makes you maintain the short distance from your target ... if you start out at short, you don't need to rush because you can reflexively move into close, hence the necessity of the reflexive move), but the Rush action cannot actually take you into close range of someone. It allows for a secondary move on your opponent's turn in order to maintain distance so that you can close the distance on your following turn. It's a bit difficult to explain.)<br /> <br /> I made this a couple of weeks ago. Maybe it can offer some help.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/Vgc-3LNznd4\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/Vgc-3LNznd4\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/Vgc-3LNznd4\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/Vgc-3LNznd4 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":482,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","user":"Ekorren","date":". 11-18-2019, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T12:54:20-08:00","id":1349418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1349346-movement-um-how#post1349346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At one point a character wanted to run from the siege weapons they'd set up on the hill outside of town (one range band/zone), through the town square (another range band/zone), and get inside the inn (a third range band/zone).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this might be part of where thinking about Range Bands like Zones might be tripping you up.<br /> <br /> In Fate, Zones each represent a distinct narrative space within the scene. Moving from one Zone to another Zone matters, regardless of the relative location of other characters.<br /> <br /> Range Bands aren't distinct spaces, just relative measures of distance.<br /> <br /> So, lets say an attacker is outside in the yard of a house, and their target is on the first floor of the house, and wants to get up to the second floor of the house because they have a weapon up there.<br /> <br /> In Fate, &quot;Front Yard, &quot;1st Floor,&quot; and &quot;2nd Floor&quot; are all Zones. The attacker in the Front Yard, is in a Zone adjacent to both of the other Zones, so attacking suffers the same issues (needs to have an attack that can cross one Zone, and can attack at someone despite walls), the target is moving Zones to take advantage of an Aspect upstairs.<br /> <br /> In Exalted, all of this is just happening at Short Range. The characters are too far apart for hand-to-hand combat, but if the attacker wanted to move into the house to be within close-combat range, they could do so relatively easily. The target running upstairs for a weapon isn't changing bands, because they're not changing the relative distance between themselves and their attacker.<br /> <br /> So something like moving from the town square into the inn would definitely be changing Zones in Fate, but probably not changing Range Bands in Exalted (if you decided it was necessary, it would most likely be a Take Cover action from the sound of it though that could get waived since you don't really need to actively duck if you're inside a building and such).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T13:29:47-08:00","id":1349430,"title":"","content":"So I don't know OPs scenario. But I picture something like this.<br /> <br /> The PCs want to defend a town. At the top of the town, on a hill are siege engines. The siege engines are at Long range from the enemy army on the plains, firing down at them. PC-1 is with the siege engines, co-ordinating the barrage.<br /> <br /> The enemy army double moving towards the siege engines is utter cheese and should not be allowed (absent Charms).<br /> <br /> Roughly the same distance away, down the hill, across the town and in an inn, PC-2 is drawing up battleplans when suddenly a traitor sets off explosives, setting the inn on fire and trying to kill PC-2. The traitor and PC-2 aren't running away, they're staying in the burning building until one of them is dead.<br /> <br /> PC-1 is at Long range from the enemy army, and Long range in the opposite direction from PC-2. PC-1 is sees the explosion and wants to help PC-2.<br /> <br /> How many turns does PC-1 have to sit and watch for until they get to play Exalted?<br /> <br /> RAW? 2. The move down the hill. Turn over. They move across the square. Turn over. They move into the building and can now play.<br /> <br /> Now let's say there's a second traitor, also at the catapult, let's call him Dash. PC-1 can Disengage from Dash. Dash wants to slow PC-1 down, so he opposes the Disengage with his Dex+Athletics vs PC-1's Dex+Dodge. PC-1 wins and moves down the hill. Dash follows, and PC-1 Reflexively moves across town. Round over. Second turn PC-1 Moves into the inn and can take part in the fight. Getting there a full turn earlier than if he did not have to contend with someone actively trying to slow him down.<br /> <br /> That's nuts. You shouldn't move at double speed if you have an enemy trying to slow you down. And your turn should be more interesting than &quot;I move. Again. And nothing happens. Again. I take no Action. Again.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1349346-movement-um-how?p=1349418#post1349418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So something like moving from the town square into the inn would definitely be changing Zones in Fate, but probably not changing Range Bands in Exalted (if you decided it was necessary, it would most likely be a Take Cover action from the sound of it though that could get waived since you don't really need to actively duck if you're inside a building and such).</div> </div> </div> </div>If I'm in the town square and you're in an inn, I don't think I could hit you with a sword unless I moved into the inn.<br /> <br /> Otherwise I agree with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-18-2019, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T13:54:17-08:00","id":1349440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1349346-movement-um-how?p=1349371#post1349371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right. Which is moving twice.<br /> <br /> The devs clarified that you only can't use the Reflexive Move (movement action) when embattled, so I guess Rushing works?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I guess I was confused because I felt your first post implied that is is the <i>Rush action </i>that let you move twice, so I wanted to clarify Rush lets you move only once, and then you have to use your own Move action (reflexive) to move again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T14:08:00-08:00","id":1349443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1349346-movement-um-how?p=1349430#post1349430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm in the town square and you're in an inn, I don't think I could hit you with a sword unless I moved into the inn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Range Bands are relative. My point was to moving away from a static ranged opponent.<br /> <br /> That said, this is Exalted, ducking into an inn doesn't mean I can't try to slash through the wall to hit you. Going into the inn is mostly dealing with the Cover rules rather than range bands, assuming moving from the square to the inn is being done via reflexive moves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T14:12:04-08:00","id":1349445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1349346-movement-um-how?p=1349440#post1349440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah I guess I was confused because I felt your first post implied that is is the <i>Rush action </i>that let you move twice, so I wanted to clarify Rush lets you move only once, and then you have to use your own Move action (reflexive) to move again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've editted to be more clear that Rush doesn't move you twice.<br /> <br /> <s>Rushing out of embattled is kinda weird though. Especially looking at the Deeb Charmset. So I've editted that too.</s><br /> <br /> [Edit]<br /> <br /> Nope, right the first time. Rush away: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1073429#post1073429\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...29#post1073429</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-18-2019, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T14:29:44-08:00","id":1349449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1349346-movement-um-how?p=1349430#post1349430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I don't know OPs scenario. But I picture something like this.<br /> <br /> The PCs want to defend a town. At the top of the town, on a hill are siege engines. The siege engines are at Long range from the enemy army on the plains, firing down at them. PC-1 is with the siege engines, co-ordinating the barrage.<br /> <br /> The enemy army double moving towards the siege engines is utter cheese and should not be allowed (absent Charms).<br /> <br /> Roughly the same distance away, down the hill, across the town and in an inn, PC-2 is drawing up battleplans when suddenly a traitor sets off explosives, setting the inn on fire and trying to kill PC-2. The traitor and PC-2 aren't running away, they're staying in the burning building until one of them is dead.<br /> <br /> PC-1 is at Long range from the enemy army, and Long range in the opposite direction from PC-2. PC-1 is sees the explosion and wants to help PC-2.<br /> <br /> How many turns does PC-1 have to sit and watch for until they get to play Exalted?<br /> <br /> RAW? 2. The move down the hill. Turn over. They move across the square. Turn over. They move into the building and can now play.<br /> <br /> Now let's say there's a second traitor, also at the catapult, let's call him Dash. PC-1 can Disengage from Dash. Dash wants to slow PC-1 down, so he opposes the Disengage with his Dex+Athletics vs PC-1's Dex+Dodge. PC-1 wins and moves down the hill. Dash follows, and PC-1 Reflexively moves across town. Round over. Second turn PC-1 Moves into the inn and can take part in the fight. Getting there a full turn earlier than if he did not have to contend with someone actively trying to slow him down.<br /> <br /> That's nuts. You shouldn't move at double speed if you have an enemy trying to slow you down. And your turn should be more interesting than &amp;quot;I move. Again. And nothing happens. Again. I take no Action. Again.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> If I'm in the town square and you're in an inn, I don't think I could hit you with a sword unless I moved into the inn.<br /> <br /> Otherwise I agree with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I struggled with that myself, especially if you try and take mounts into account with crossing from long range in combat time.<br /> <br /> To clear up the siege engine to inn scenario, while your disengage does keep from being in Close with Dash, it doesn't necessarily get you to where you are going faster, since it's relative. Wibbly Wobbly Rangey Bandey to paraphrase The Doctor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T14:36:59-08:00","id":1349450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1349346-movement-um-how?p=1349449#post1349449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I struggled with that myself, especially if you try and take mounts into account with crossing from long range in combat time.<br /> <br /> To clear up the siege engine to inn scenario, while your disengage does keep from being in Close with Dash, it doesn't necessarily get you to where you are going faster, since it's relative. Wibbly Wobbly Rangey Bandey to paraphrase The Doctor.</div> </div> </div> </div>As well as Dash there's a third traitor, Archer, in the town square, Medium range to the inn and siege engines.<br /> <br /> When you Disengage down the hill, you're now Short range from Dash and one range band closer to Archer, and when Dash follows you, you can Reflexively move into Close with Archer.<br /> <br /> Again, you shouldn't get faster when you add more enemies.<br /> <br /> It really is neater just to accept that you can move two range bands in a round if you use up your Combat Action to do it, and you're not cheesing your way around the combat mechanics. IMHO. YMMV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T15:35:24-08:00","id":1349457,"title":"","content":"And of course, as long as you're not actively fighting, Racing Hare Method lets you cross <i>three</i> range bands per turn. Or you can use Mountain-Crossing Leap Technique for a quick Hulk jump to cross four range bands in an instant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T15:43:58-08:00","id":1349460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1349346-movement-um-how?p=1349450#post1349450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As well as Dash there's a third traitor, Archer, in the town square, Medium range to the inn and siege engines.<br /> <br /> When you Disengage down the hill, you're now Short range from Dash and one range band closer to Archer, and when Dash follows you, you can Reflexively move into Close with Archer.<br /> <br /> Again, you shouldn't get faster when you add more enemies.<br /> <br /> It really is neater just to accept that you can move two range bands in a round if you use up your Combat Action to do it, and you're not cheesing your way around the combat mechanics. IMHO. YMMV.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree, I toyed with something similar that when you rush you get your free movement at the end of the round if your target doesn't move. I also toyed with combining that with allowing mounted combatants to Rush from Medium. People balked at that pretty hard, if only because people thought a horse giving you the equivalent of a Solar Athletics charm was antithetical to some.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T16:08:09-08:00","id":1349461,"title":"","content":"So... how do you guys handle positioning and movement at the table? Pure theater of the mind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T16:16:58-08:00","id":1349464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1349346-movement-um-how?p=1349461#post1349461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... how do you guys handle positioning and movement at the table? Pure theater of the mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much, yes. Sometimes if a player is having trouble understanding I'll get out a dry-erase board and draw some X's on it, but otherwise it tends to be pretty easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T16:44:32-08:00","id":1349466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1349346-movement-um-how?p=1349461#post1349461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... how do you guys handle positioning and movement at the table? Pure theater of the mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Here's something vaguely resembling a map of the relevant landmarks. Put your minis (er, distinctively colored dice) wherever you areish. Yes, areish. This ain't exact. Movement is an art, not a science, so feel free to ask before you move.&quot;<br /> If I had more time, I'd overlay a map with a set of nodes and lines between them. One line between nodes = one range band. Sharing a node is Close.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T17:36:16-08:00","id":1349471,"title":"","content":"I've always wondered how you would simulate the running sideways sword fight with 3rd's movement rules, because neither party is actively trying to disengage, but the are moving relative to the rest of the 'fight'<br /> <br /> Vid for context<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?time_continue=13&amp;v=5jYbRscI0RU&amp;feature=emb_title\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?time_continue=13&amp;v=5jYbRscI0RU&amp;feature=emb_title\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?time_continue=13&amp;v=5jYbRscI0RU&amp;feature=emb_title\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?time_continue=13&amp;v=5jYbRscI0RU&amp;feature=emb_title </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11701-fiikragg","name":"Fiikragg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11701_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T17:40:48-08:00","id":1349474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1349346-movement-um-how?p=1349461#post1349461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... how do you guys handle positioning and movement at the table? Pure theater of the mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>In regular battles theater of the mind works well enough for me. However if I'm running a large scale battle then I throw the &quot;dramatic&quot; range bands out the window and use a D&amp;D/pathfinder style grid instead, assigning the following values for range bands :<ul><li>Close = 10ft</li> <li>Short = 30ft</li> <li>Medium = 60ft</li> <li>Long = 100ft</li> <li>Extreme = 150ft</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T23:28:34-08:00","id":1349503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fiikragg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1349346-movement-um-how?p=1349471#post1349471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always wondered how you would simulate the running sideways sword fight with 3rd's movement rules, because neither party is actively trying to disengage, but the are moving relative to the rest of the 'fight'<br /> <br /> Vid for context<br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?time_continue=13&amp;v=5jYbRscI0RU&amp;feature=emb_title\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?time_c...ture=emb_title</a></div> </div> </div> </div>If there are other combatants who can't keep pace, then disengage and rush. One party Disengages to short, the other Rushes, then moves to Close, disengage moves to Short again, rush brings them close again. So they end up at close range to each other, Medium range from where they were.<br /> <br /> If there aren't other combatants who can't follow them, then just narrate the movement with Stunts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T23:46:25-08:00","id":1349507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fiikragg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1349346-movement-um-how?p=1349471#post1349471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always wondered how you would simulate the running sideways sword fight with 3rd's movement rules, because neither party is actively trying to disengage, but the are moving relative to the rest of the 'fight'</div> </div> </div> </div>I houserule the &quot;no moving if embattled&quot; rule to &quot;no moving if embattled unless all your opponents say OK&quot;. So a moving sword fight is as simple as one party wanting it and the other not minding.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T23:48:19-08:00","id":1349508,"title":"","content":"My god these rules still annoy me. They're one of those things I try to dodge when bringing up EX3 with potential new players - range bands are fine but rush and disengage are complex enough that when my group had a key misunderstanding about disengage (that you can go anywhere on the field for free without a disengage, the opponent just having to move to keep up) I couldn't bring myself to fight for RAW too hard.<br /> <br /> I always theatre of the mind this stuff, and with two combatants locked in melee, I let stunt description and success dictate movement. The character winning the fight controls where you gom","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4086,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","user":"Croakamancer","date":". 11-19-2019, 02:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T01:12:15-08:00","id":1349523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1349346-movement-um-how?p=1349445#post1349445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've editted to be more clear that Rush doesn't move you twice.<br /> <br /> <s>Rushing out of embattled is kinda weird though. Especially looking at the Deeb Charmset. So I've editted that too.</s><br /> <br /> [Edit]<br /> <br /> Nope, right the first time. Rush away: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1073429#post1073429\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...29#post1073429</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the link I have been wondering for some time now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T02:35:39-08:00","id":1349532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1349346-movement-um-how?p=1349461#post1349461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... how do you guys handle positioning and movement at the table? Pure theater of the mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually the fight is sufficiently bidimensional, like fighting on the street or just two or three actors working similarly. So &quot;where they are&quot;, &quot;where they were&quot; and &quot;where they will be&quot; are just 3 connected-ish places. <br /> To me that's easy to just commit to memory, same for the players.<br /> If it gets more complex than that I bust a glass hexagon board and some markers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T04:56:28-08:00","id":1349542,"title":"","content":"Saw a pretty neat chart last week with a bunch of interconnected segments to represent different range bands. Like you put two people in the same one they're at close range, two adjacent ones they're at short, if there's a space between them they're at medium and so on. It was set up so that you could have various groups at different ranges from each other and keep it all consistent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 11-19-2019, 07:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T05:05:49-08:00","id":1349546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1349346-movement-um-how?p=1349508#post1349508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My god these rules still annoy me. They're one of those things I try to dodge when bringing up EX3 with potential new players - range bands are fine but rush and disengage are complex enough that when my group had a key misunderstanding about disengage (that you can go anywhere on the field for free without a disengage, the opponent just having to move to keep up) I couldn't bring myself to fight for RAW too hard.<br /> <br /> I always theatre of the mind this stuff, and with two combatants locked in melee, I let stunt description and success dictate movement. The character winning the fight controls where you gom</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the rule though, isn't it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Disengage (Combat Action): This action must be taken when a character at close range with one or more hostile opponents <b>wishes to retreat</b> to short range\u2014the standard reflexive move action cannot be used to do so. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T05:35:54-08:00","id":1349549,"title":"","content":"The movement system is probably my biggest gripe with 3E. It has got to be one of the only systems where there is no way to spend your entire action on movement to squeeze out more distance without having access to charms to do so. It really limits options, and in my opinion, Rush should just allow an extra range band of movement instead of being a reflexive anti-kite move, and the charms that allow Rush to do just that should have done something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25108-ikeulhu","name":"ikeulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T07:49:16-08:00","id":1349588,"title":"","content":"I've been running Edge of the Empire a bit. That uses range bands as well (which are important due to the accuracy penalties for longer range) and you can swap your attack for a second move, or take 2 strain (which is non-lethal damage). There's also rules for chases.<br /> I haven't had any issues with it so far.<br /> Tbh I don't love the system (because of the special dice, and I find the combats a bit dull), but that seems fine.<br /> <br /> The way the Exalted movement rules are designed is 99% about stopping kiting. And it does that well, honestly. But I think there was probably some easier solutions.<br /> <br /> (No-one kites in Warhammer. Except horse archers, who are supposed to. You just have to say &quot;you can't run away and then shoot a bow behind you while doing it, that's ridiculous&quot;.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T07:54:32-08:00","id":1349589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1349346-movement-um-how?p=1349546#post1349546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is the rule though, isn't it?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sample situation. Guard is standing in the middle of a street, trying to bar passage. Thief closes to close range, but next round wants to move. RAW I read that as a no go - thief'd have to use disengage. But the interpretation I'm looking at says that's fine - the Guard would have to use reflexive to keep up, even without disengage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T09:30:19-08:00","id":1349599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1349346-movement-um-how?p=1349588#post1349588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way the Exalted movement rules are designed is 99% about stopping kiting. And it does that well, honestly. But I think there was probably some easier solutions.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was probably a more elegant way to do it, but the system actually doesn\u2019t stop kiting, it makes you have to work for it. Kiting is 100% a viable strategy in Ex3, you just need good Dex, athletics and dodge, and a mount if you can swing it. It\u2019s why you can\u2019t use your action to double move If you ever tried to kite your foe could just double move into you and lock you down in Close range again. <br /> <br /> On the other hand it screws with the heads of new players and leads to really weird cases where you become twice as fast while fleeing or chasing somebody, which makes no sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T10:01:25-08:00","id":1349606,"title":"","content":"What if...<br /> <br /> *Disengage moves you one Range Band, with no follow-up movement if, well, followed. (That gets you 2 bands away with your reflexive move added)<br /> *Rush moves you one Range Band as your action, and if you move into Close range with a foe, you have to make the opposed Dex+Athletics check. If you fail, your target can retreat 1 band reflexively. (That gets you 2 bands away with your reflexive move added, but allows a fast enemy to keep distance),<br /> <br /> That seems like it'll be <i>pretty </i>close to RAW while being a lot easier to make sense of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T10:23:28-08:00","id":1349613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1349346-movement-um-how?p=1349599#post1349599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There was probably a more elegant way to do it, but the system actually doesn\u2019t stop kiting, it makes you have to work for it. Kiting is 100% a viable strategy in Ex3, you just need good Dex, athletics and dodge, and a mount if you can swing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... you have to flurry though, giving you -3 attack dice and -1 defence, right?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T10:29:30-08:00","id":1349616,"title":"","content":"I think that would be okay. The dynamic is slightly different, a successful disengage needs to be followed by a successful contest of a rush to get your ranged attacks in, and you\u2019d have to rework the rush and disengage charms but I can\u2019t see anything really broken with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T10:31:19-08:00","id":1349617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1349346-movement-um-how?p=1349613#post1349613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... you have to flurry though, giving you -3 attack dice and -1 defence, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>No need to flurry. You spend your action to disengage and move to short, and now once at short the enemy can\u2019t close to Close again, because if he tries to move towards you then you move back. Then next turn you get to shoot without flurrying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T13:05:03-08:00","id":1349654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1349346-movement-um-how?p=1349616#post1349616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that would be okay. The dynamic is slightly different, a successful disengage needs to be followed by a successful contest of a rush to get your ranged attacks in, and you\u2019d have to rework the rush and disengage charms but I can\u2019t see anything really broken with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... looking at charms...<ul><li>Lightning Speed seems fine</li> <li>Racing Hare Method seems fine</li> <li>Onrush Burst Method is fine</li> <li>Arete-Driven Marathon Stance seems fine</li> <li>Demon-Wasting Rush... doesn't really work literally, but seems easy to fix with an interpretive reading (&quot;you can rush two range bands&quot;)</li> <li>Hurricane Sprint Speed works fine</li> <li>Godspeed Steps works fine</li> <li>Living Wind Approach works fine</li> <li>Dust Motes Whirling works fine</li> <li>Shadow Dancer Method almost works; again, a less literal reading (&quot;you disengage and come back&quot;) has no issue.</li> <li>Fleet Dreaming Image... actually, I can't tell what this is for in the first place. You don't need to Disengage if you're already at short range?</li> <li>Sunlight Bleeding Away... as with Demon-Wasting Rush, it's easy enough to see what it should be under new rules (&quot;move two range bands when you disengage)</li> <li>Elusive Mount Technique works fine</li> <li>Untouchable Horseman's Attitude works fine</li> <li>Coursing Firebolt Flash works fine</li> <li>Phantom Rider's Approach can become &quot;move two range bands when you disengage&quot;</li> <li>Soaring Pegasus Style works fine</li> </ul>So... yeah, minimum impact?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T13:35:17-08:00","id":1349666,"title":"","content":"Fleet Dreaming Image means you can Disengage at Short, then when they try to move to Close, you immediately move back to Short. Plus it's Reflexive, so you can Attack at Short range, then when you're advanced on, stay at Short range (unless you're successfully Rushed).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T14:03:42-08:00","id":1349681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1349346-movement-um-how?p=1349617#post1349617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No need to flurry. You spend your action to disengage and move to short, and now once at short the enemy can\u2019t close to Close again, because if he tries to move towards you then you move back. Then next turn you get to shoot without flurrying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but then he can just charge you on the following turn and attack, can't he? So you end up making one attack for each of his attacks anyway. Plus, if he moves towards close and you jump back to short, he's got an action with nothing to do, so he might as well rush you so you can't flee the next turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T14:13:13-08:00","id":1349684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1349346-movement-um-how?p=1349681#post1349681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but then he can just charge you on the following turn and attack, can't he? So you end up making one attack for each of his attacks anyway. Plus, if he moves towards close and you jump back to short, he's got an action with nothing to do, so he might as well rush you so you can't flee the next turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, in the first round yes he can move, you jump back, and he can rush. If he wins, you still get your one shot off, but you lost the rush so next turn he\u2019ll get back into close for his shot. If he either doesn\u2019t move or fails the rush, then you shoot and move back on your turn. Now you\u2019re at medium range, and the best he can do is follow you and rush. If he fails, shoot and retreat to medium. He follows and attempts to rush, if he fails, shoot and retreat ect.<br /> <br /> If he WINS then he gets his free shot next round, you can flee, advance, stay still, he\u2019s getting there for his shot. Then on your turn you can disengage and try to start the chance again. Charms obviously change this, some charms let you rush in instantly from range, others like Wind Dragon Speed give you no penalty for flurrying an attack with disengage, so you might as well do it anyway. <br /> <br /> <br /> The other thing he can do is just not move on the second turn or retreat to Long range, but staying at a range that you can\u2019t attack from is not a pathway to victory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}